min` is not among them: minting epochs, admitting and removing members are the community\'s, as the room\'s owner, and are exercised through the vtc/rooms/community/* tasks rather than by any member\'s credential. `curate` is not implied by `write`."},"RoomDescription":{"title":"RoomDescription","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"What the room is for, in a sentence or a short paragraph, written by an administrator: shown to administrators holding `vtc.rooms.manage` and to the members the room is offered to. Plain text — a consumer renders it as text, never as markup. Like `RoomLabel`, it is the community\'s own record as the room\'s owner: not part of the room\'s identity and never in anything a room\'s host can read. From `vtc/rooms/community/create` 0.3 and `vtc/rooms/community/update` 0.2 the community also writes it, through its own VTA, as the `description` of the room\'s own profile (`RoomProfile` in rooms/_shared), sealed inside the room for its members; earlier versions keep it out of the room altogether. It MUST NOT carry personal data or a credential, and a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"RoomLabel":{"title":"RoomLabel","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"A name for the room, chosen by an administrator: shown to administrators and to the members a room is offered to. Not part of the room\'s identity and never in anything a room\'s host can read. From `vtc/rooms/community/create` 0.3 and `vtc/rooms/community/update` 0.2 the community also writes it, through its own VTA, as the `name` of the room\'s own profile (`RoomProfile` in rooms/_shared), sealed inside the room for its members; earlier versions keep it out of the room altogether. MUST NOT carry personal data."},"Visibility":{"title":"Visibility","type":"string","enum":["open","attributed","private"],"description":"How much of a room its host can see, fixed at creation and immutable thereafter. `open`: records are cleartext, searchable and fully audited. `attributed`: record content is sealed, and the host still learns which member acted. `private`: content is sealed and membership is presented in zero knowledge, so the host verifies that a member acted without learning which. Immutable because a downgrade cannot un-see cleartext and an upgrade would protect only what came after while presenting as though it protected everything."},"OfferV2":{"title":"OfferV2","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["roomId","host","label","visibility","actions","validUntil","offeredAt","state","credentials"],"description":"What vtc/rooms/offers/list/0.2 returns: `Offer` plus `description`. A separate definition, not a change to `Offer`, so that vtc/rooms/offers/list/0.1 keeps the exact shape it published. `label` and `description` are the room\'s as they stand when the offer is read, not as they stood when it was made.","properties":{"roomId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":512},"host":{"type":"string","pattern":"^did:","maxLength":2048,"description":"The room\'s host: this community."},"label":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RoomLabel"},"description":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RoomDescription","description":"Absent when the room has none."},"visibility":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Visibility"},"actions":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MemberActions"},"validUntil":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"offeredAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"state":{"type":"string","enum":["open","accepted"],"description":"`open`: not yet accepted. `accepted`: accepted, kept listed while a repeated accept can still be answered."},"credentials":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/OfferCredentials"}}},"OfferCredentials":{"title":"OfferCredentials","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["invitation","membership","authority"],"description":"The three credentials the room issued to the member, serialized as rooms/owner/{invite,issue-membership,issue-authority} return them. None is a secret: each names its subject, and a presentation of it must be signed by that subject. The member stores them in their own key holder\'s vault.","properties":{"invitation":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":65536,"description":"The Verifiable Invitation Credential. On a sealed tier the member\'s key holder needs it to mint a KeyPackage (rooms/keys/key-package) and to accept the Welcome (rooms/keys/welcome)."},"membership":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":65536,"description":"The Verifiable Membership Credential."},"authority":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":65536,"description":"The Verifiable Authority Credential granting `actions` until `validUntil`."}}}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
